// Retire MCP runtimes (the agentmemory shim) after 30 minutes without use.
// Why it was tried: since the Max lane (2026-11-16) main and deep run on claude-cli, and every
// isolated heartbeat run leaves its agentmemory shim and the shim's process-group anchor running,
// about 146 MB a pair, two pairs an hour (1.46 GB by 11:45 on 2026-11-17).
// Applied 2026-11-17 16:45 by hot reload. It did NOT stop that leak: the 16:55 heartbeat's shims
// were still running 42 idle minutes later. The idle sweep skips runtimes that hold a lease, and
// claude-cli keeps up to 16 "live sessions" registered (see docs/runbooks/jorah-on-pc.md,
// "Memory leak and voice warm-up"). Kept as a guard for runtimes nothing holds.
// Cost: a session idle for 30 minutes may reconnect the shim on its next turn. Data is unaffected:
// the shim only proxies to the agentmemory service on 127.0.0.1:47300.
// Undo: `config unset mcp.sessionIdleTtlMs` (back to no idle eviction). Backup openclaw.json.pre-mcp-idle.
{
  mcp: {
    sessionIdleTtlMs: 1800000,
  },
}
